  m_text: In 1963, Ford tried to buy Ferrari, but Enzo Ferrari walked away from the
    deal. Henry Ford II then set out to beat Ferrari at the 24 Hours of Le Mans,
    and the GT40 was the result. It won Le Mans four years in a row, from 1966 to
    1969, and got its name from being only 40 inches tall. Ford revived the idea
    for its 100th anniversary with this modern Ford GT, which has a mid-mounted supercharged
    5.4L V8.
