  m_text: The Nissan Silvia name dates back to 1965, but the S15 became the final
    generation of the series. Introduced in 1999, it was a lightweight, rear-wheel-drive
    sports coupe designed around simplicity and driver involvement. The performance-oriented
    Spec-R used Nissan's turbocharged 2.0L SR20DET engine. Its rear-wheel-drive layout,
    relatively low weight, and responsive chassis made it popular among driving enthusiasts
    and helped establish the S15 as an important car in Japan's drifting culture.
    The example displayed here features a Vertex Edge widebody kit, a popular aftermarket
    modification.
