  m_text: The Toyota Supra began in 1978 as a larger and more powerful version of
    the Celica. The fourth-generation A80 Supra, introduced in 1993, represented
    a major step toward becoming a dedicated performance car. Its most famous engine
    was the 3.0L twin-turbocharged 2JZ-GTE inline-six. The engine's strong iron block
    and robust design gave it considerable tuning potential, helping establish the
    Supra as a legend among performance enthusiasts. Its worldwide popularity grew
    even further after an orange Supra appeared in the 2001 film The Fast and the
    Furious.
